  "summary": "Prove two sequential action lifecycles in one Shop history.",
  "why": "Luis approved an optional one-active-action profile using the existing interpreter, with a separate Shop correction between lifecycles. The profile preserves cumulative indexes and records, adds current pointers, binds payload hashes to retained bytes and requires observation of the current action before a successor. A negative probe found an old-execution/new-contract gate bypass, now closed by binding observation through execution and dispatch to the current action. Two RED commits preceded integration. Final sequential tests: 13 passed; original Shop-action, owning-history and keyed-effect regression: 45 passed. The run has 106 events, five KCS, one revision and two complete recorded lifecycles. Fresh-process replay denies research/test imports. Source registration precedes atomic context/proposal. Effect and observation inputs are synthetic. No runtime, ontology, package, original profile, historical receipt, paper or downstream change; no migration, new instruction, concurrency, SDK, full-repository GREEN, release or push claim.",
